# 0.4.0 step 2: a restart while a summary call runs. A run ends at ~155K and settle starts the summary the warm return would make
# (rule A); in a slow world it takes 2 minutes, so pi restarts while it runs: the call is lost (recorded as one unused call, its cost
# kept). The prompt 60 s later finds the cache warm and nothing ready: the restarted process decides as a fresh one (RD, RDr) and,
# with a UI, writes the summary in the background instead of making the user wait (A3; 0.3.0 waited at req 14).
world explicit known ttl=300 true=300 survival=none c=1 sys=3000 window=200000 native interactive slow
prompt
say 150K
prompt +1h
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
call npm 100
say 100
restart
prompt +60s
say 100
